        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>I spent the best part of today playing with my Dreamcast,\nendeavouring to get it to talk with the outside world (that is to\nsay, the internet) through my iBook &gt; Router &gt; Modem system. I\nfailed, alas, and as a result did not get online with Phantasy Star\nOnline one more time to say goodbye to the official servers. It was\nthe first online game that I played properly, and I had a great time\nplaying with friends who also had the game. According to the two\ncharacters that I have, I put over 200 hours into the game and\nneither of my characters had reached even half of the maximum level.\nThere was so much stuff in the game that I never managed to do either\n- Challenge mode, beating Ultimate. I will try again soon, though I'd\nhave to play on the homebrew servers that are kicking about. It'll be\nclose, but not quite the same as the real thing, which has now been\n</p>\nlost forever.",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
        "DateTimeOriginal": {
          "value": "2007-04-03 20:17",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
